# Governance Proposal: Fix Willow Noticed Dashboard Card

**Proposer:** Ganesha (Claude Code CLI / Sonnet 4.6)
**Date:** 2026-02-28T06:00:00Z
**Type:** Bug Fix
**Trust Level:** ENGINEER (3)

## Summary
Three bugs prevent the Willow Noticed card from displaying connection proposals on the
SAFE dashboard. (1) loadConnections() doesn't unwrap the API envelope — API returns
{"connections":[...]} but JS expects a bare array, so the card always shows empty.
(2) buildConnectionCard() uses wrong field names — API returns name_a/name_b but JS
looks for entity_a/entity_b, so entity names never render. (3) loadWillowKnows() is
called on page load and on refresh but is never defined, causing a silent JS error that
aborts further rendering. All three are one-line fixes plus adding the missing function.

## Proposed Changes
**File:** SAFE/web/dashboard.html
**Location:** loadConnections() (~line 600), buildConnectionCard() (~line 616), missing loadWillowKnows()

## Rationale
- Dashboard shows blank "Willow Noticed" section despite 134 confirmed + pending connections in DB
- Root cause: API response envelope mismatch + missing function definition
- No architecture change — pure bug fix, zero new dependencies

## Risk Assessment
- **Risk Level:** MINIMAL
- **Reversible:** YES
- **Dependencies:** None
- **Testing:** Reload dashboard → Willow Noticed card shows pending connections; Scan button triggers POST /api/willow/scan-connections

## ΔE Impact
Expected ΔE: +0.050 (dashboard becomes functional — low delta, but unlocks Willow's proposal loop)

## Implementation
```python
path = r"C:/Users/Sean/Documents/GitHub/SAFE/web/dashboard.html"
with open(path, "r", encoding="utf-8") as f:
    content = f.read()

# Fix 1: Unwrap API envelope in loadConnections()
content = content.replace(
    "    const connections = await res.json();\n\n    if (!Array.isArray(connections) || connections.length === 0) {",
    "    const data = await res.json();\n    const connections = data.connections || [];\n\n    if (connections.length === 0) {"
)

# Fix 2: Correct field names in buildConnectionCard()
content = content.replace(
    "  const entityA = escHtml(c.entity_a || c.source || '?');\n  const entityB = escHtml(c.entity_b || c.target || '?');\n  const reason  = escHtml(c.reason || c.description || '');",
    "  const entityA = escHtml(c.name_a || '?');\n  const entityB = escHtml(c.name_b || '?');\n  const reason  = escHtml(c.connection_type || c.reason || '');"
)

# Fix 3: Add missing loadWillowKnows() function
# Insert after the closing brace of loadConnections() (after the catch block)
old_anchor = "// ── Pigeon Mail ────────────────────────────────────────────"
new_func = '''async function loadWillowKnows() {
  const el = document.getElementById('willowKnowsContainer');
  if (!el) return;
  el.innerHTML =
    '<div style="display:flex;gap:0.5rem;align-items:center;margin-top:0.5rem">' +
    '<button class="btn-willow-test" onclick="triggerWillowScan()" id="btnWillowScan">Scan for connections</button>' +
    '<span id="willowScanResult" style="font-size:12px;color:var(--fg-muted)"></span>' +
    '</div>';
}

async function triggerWillowScan() {
  const btn = document.getElementById('btnWillowScan');
  const result = document.getElementById('willowScanResult');
  if (btn) btn.textContent = 'Scanning…';
  try {
    const res = await fetch(getWillowBase() + '/api/willow/scan-connections', { method: 'POST' });
    const data = await res.json();
    if (btn) btn.textContent = 'Scan for connections';
    if (result) result.textContent = data.new_proposals > 0
      ? data.new_proposals + ' new proposals found'
      : 'No new connections found';
    if (data.new_proposals > 0) loadConnections();
  } catch (e) {
    if (btn) btn.textContent = 'Scan for connections';
    if (result) result.textContent = 'Willow offline';
  }
}

'''
content = content.replace(old_anchor, new_func + old_anchor)

with open(path, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
    f.write(content)

# Verify
with open(path, "r", encoding="utf-8") as f:
    check = f.read()

ok1 = "data.connections || []" in check
ok2 = "c.name_a" in check
ok3 = "async function loadWillowKnows" in check
print(f"Fix 1 (envelope unwrap): {'OK' if ok1 else 'FAILED'}")
print(f"Fix 2 (field names): {'OK' if ok2 else 'FAILED'}")
print(f"Fix 3 (loadWillowKnows): {'OK' if ok3 else 'FAILED'}")
```

